---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What comes with the $7 Meal Deal at Dairy Queen?', a: 'The $7 Meal Deal includes an entrée (an Original Cheeseburger or 3-piece chicken strips), regular fries, a soft drink and a small sundae. It is offered all day at participating DQ Grill & Chill restaurants.' },
  { q: 'What is on the DQ 2 for $5 menu?', a: 'You pick any two eligible items for $5. Common choices include 2-piece chicken strips, a cheeseburger, a chili cheese dog, pretzel sticks with queso, fries and a small sundae. The list varies by store.' },
  { q: 'Does Dairy Queen have a 2 for $7 deal?', a: 'Some markets run a 2 for $7 menu with larger items, either instead of or alongside 2 for $5. Check the DQ app or your store’s menu board.' },
  { q: 'Can you swap the sundae in the $7 Meal Deal for a Blizzard?', a: 'Many stores let you upgrade the sundae to a Mini Blizzard for an extra charge. Ask at the counter, because it depends on the location.' },
  { q: 'Is there an $8 meal deal at Dairy Queen?', a: 'Some locations charge more than $7 for the meal deal or offer a different bundle. Local franchises set their own prices, so check your store’s menu board or the DQ app.' },
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="Dairy Queen $7 Meal Deal, 2 for $5 & 2 for $7 Guide"
  description="Dairy Queen $7 Meal Deal, 2 for $5 and 2 for $7 explained: what is included, typical prices, availability and the best picks."
  h1="Dairy Queen Meal Deals: $7 Meal, 2 for $5 and 2 for $7"
  crumb="DQ Meal Deals"
  eyebrow="Value deals at DQ"
  image="/Images/7-meal-deal.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen $7 Meal Deal trays with cheeseburgers, chicken strips, fries, drinks and sundaes"
  datePublished="2026-03-05"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p class="lead"><strong>The Dairy Queen $7 Meal Deal gets you an entrée, fries, a drink and a small sundae for $7.</strong> You choose an Original Cheeseburger or 3-piece chicken strips. DQ also runs a 2 for $5 Mix &amp; Match menu, and some areas have a 2 for $7 version with bigger items. Below is what each deal includes and how to get the most from it.</p>

  <h2 id="at-a-glance">DQ value deals at a glance</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Deal</th><th>What you get</th><th>Price</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a></strong></td><td>Cheeseburger or 3-piece strips, regular fries, soft drink, small sundae</td><td class="price-cell">$7.00</td><td>Participating DQ Grill &amp; Chill, all day</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/2-for-5-mix-match">2 for $5 Mix &amp; Match</a></strong></td><td>Any two eligible items</td><td class="price-cell">$5.00</td><td>Participating locations; item list varies</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>2 for $7</strong></td><td>Any two eligible larger items</td><td class="price-cell">$7.00</td><td>Some markets only</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="seven-dollar-meal">What comes with the $7 Meal Deal?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Entrée:</strong> an <a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">Original Cheeseburger</a> or 3-piece chicken strips.</li>
    <li><strong>Side:</strong> <a href="/items/regular-fries">regular fries</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Drink:</strong> a soft drink.</li>
    <li><strong>Dessert:</strong> a small sundae, such as <a href="/items/hot-fudge-sundae">hot fudge</a> or <a href="/items/strawberry-sundae">strawberry</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The cheeseburger meal is about 950 calories and the chicken strip meal about 1,010. Bought one by one, the same items cost a lot more than $7, which makes this one of the better-value meals in fast food.</p>

  <h3>Chicken strips or cheeseburger?</h3>
  <p>Pick the chicken strips if you want the most food. DQ’s strips are whole chicken breast and filling. Pick the cheeseburger if you want the lighter meal.</p>

  <h2 id="two-for-five">The 2 for $5 Mix &amp; Match menu</h2>
  <p>Choose any two items from the <a href="/items/2-for-5-mix-match">2 for $5 menu</a> for $5 total. Items you will often see:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/items/2pc-chicken-strips">2-piece chicken strips</a></li>
    <li><a href="/items/original-cheeseburger">Cheeseburger</a></li>
    <li><a href="/items/chili-cheese-dog">Chili cheese dog</a></li>
    <li><a href="/items/pretzel-sticks-queso">Pretzel sticks with queso</a></li>
    <li>Regular fries or a small sundae</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Best picks:</strong> the chicken strips and pretzel sticks with queso, because they cost the most when ordered on their own. Fries are the weakest pick, since they are already cheap.</p>

  <h2 id="two-for-seven">The DQ 2 for $7 deal</h2>
  <p>Some Dairy Queen markets run a <strong>2 for $7</strong> menu instead of, or next to, 2 for $5. It works the same way, but the items are bigger. To check, open the DQ app, choose your store and look under Deals, or ask at the counter. If your store has both, 2 for $5 is better for a snack and 2 for $7 for a full meal.</p>

  <h2 id="tips">Tips to get more from DQ meal deals</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Upgrade the sundae.</strong> Many stores will swap it for a <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Mini Blizzard</a> for a small charge.</li>
    <li><strong>Add Texas toast.</strong> The strip meal does not include it, but you can add a slice.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the app first.</strong> App-only deals sometimes beat the menu board. See our <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-app-rewards-hacks">DQ app rewards guide</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Feeding kids?</strong> Compare with the <a href="/categories/kids-meals">DQ kids meals</a>.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>For every current deal and combo in one place, see our <a href="/combos">Dairy Queen deals page</a>.</p>
</BlogPost>
